<title>USA: Regent Bancshares Q1 net loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Regent Bancshares Q1 net loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							   March 31,</p>
<p>						1997		     1996</p>
<p> Net Interest Income		    1,590		   2,056</p>
<p> Provision for Loan Losses	    (200)		     175</p>
<p> Net Income				 (180)		     218</p>
<p> Net Income Per Share		  $(.20)		    $.05</p>
<p>Weighted Average Primary</p>
<p>   Common Shares Outstanding	  1,343		   1,358</p>
<p>		     (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Regent Bancshares Corp said its net interest income in the first quarter of l997 was 23 percent lower than the same period last year due to a strategically planned decrease in earning assets of 27 percent that was necessary to improve the bank's regulatory capital ratios at that time.</p>
<p>Net income included more than $700,000 in gains realized on the sale of $34.2 million in loan participations.</p>
<p>The provision for loan losses was reported as a benefit of $200 thousand in the first quarter of this year versus an expense of $175 thousand in the comparable quarter of 1996.</p>
</text>
